{
  "formatVersion": 4,
  "name": "ssd1306-text",
  "target": "esp32-s3",
  "targets": [
    "esp32-s3",
    "rp2040-pico",
    "simulator"
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "name": "Main",
      "periodMs": 50
    },
    {
      "name": "init",
      "periodMs": 0,
      "kind": "init"
    }
  ],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "btn_count",
      "type": "digital-input",
      "name": "CountButton"
    },
    {
      "id": "btn_reset",
      "type": "digital-input",
      "name": "ResetButton"
    },
    {
      "id": "cnt",
      "type": "counter",
      "properties": {
        "presetCount": "1000"
      },
      "comment": "An up-counter. CU increments CV on each rising edge of CountButton; R (ResetButton) clears it and is reset-dominant. presetCount (1000) is the ceiling. CV is the live count, which gets formatted and shown on the OLED."
    },
    {
      "id": "count_text",
      "type": "to-text",
      "properties": {
        "type": "int32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "oled_count",
      "type": "ssd1306-text",
      "name": "Oled",
      "properties": {
        "col": "0",
        "line": "2"
      },
      "comment": "On Main, so it refreshes every 50 ms. It has no 'text' property; instead its 'text' input port is driven by the live count, so line 2 keeps updating. The static labels above set 'text' as a fixed property instead - property = constant, port = live."
    },
    {
      "id": "n1",
      "type": "ssd1306-text",
      "name": "Oled",
      "task": "init",
      "properties": {
        "col": "0",
        "line": "0",
        "text": "Hello SMFlow!"
      },
      "comment": "task: init. The 'init' task (kind: init, periodMs 0) runs once at startup, not on a period - so this static label is painted a single time. All three of these nodes name the one 'Oled' peripheral (declared under 'peripherals', an SSD1306 over I2C); they are just views onto the same display at different lines."
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "type": "ssd1306-text",
      "name": "Oled",
      "task": "init",
      "properties": {
        "col": "0",
        "line": "4",
        "text": "Status: OK"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "doc_overview",
      "type": "comment",
      "name": "What this shows",
      "comment": "Two tasks working together. 'init' runs once at boot to paint the static 'Hello SMFlow!' and 'Status: OK' labels; 'Main' runs every 50 ms to show a live, button-driven count. Everything prints to one named peripheral, Oled (an SSD1306 over I2C). Notice the flow never names an I2C bus or address - that binding lives in ssd1306-text.iomap. This is the first sample with both a dedicated init task and an external peripheral."
    }
  ],
  "connections": [
    {
      "from": {
        "node": "btn_count",
        "port": "value"
      },
      "to": {
        "node": "cnt",
        "port": "CU"
      }
    },
    {
      "from": {
        "node": "btn_reset",
        "port": "value"
      },
      "to": {
        "node": "cnt",
        "port": "R"
      }
    },
    {
      "from": {
        "node": "cnt",
        "port": "CV"
      },
      "to": {
        "node": "count_text",
        "port": "value"
      }
    },
    {
      "from": {
        "node": "count_text",
        "port": "text"
      },
      "to": {
        "node": "oled_count",
        "port": "text"
      }
    }
  ],
  "hardware": [
    {
      "logical": "CountButton",
      "direction": "input",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "logical": "ResetButton",
      "direction": "input",
      "type": "bool"
    }
  ],
  "peripherals": [
    {
      "name": "Oled",
      "type": "solomon:ssd1306"
    }
  ],
  "ui": {
    "nodes": {
      "doc_overview": {
        "x": 40,
        "y": 400
      },
      "btn_count": {
        "x": 40,
        "y": 160
      },
      "btn_reset": {
        "x": 40,
        "y": 280
      },
      "cnt": {
        "x": 260,
        "y": 200
      },
      "count_text": {
        "x": 460,
        "y": 200
      },
      "n1": {
        "x": 64,
        "y": 64
      },
      "n2": {
        "x": 64.80000000000001,
        "y": 191.19999999999993
      },
      "oled_count": {
        "x": 700,
        "y": 200
      }
    }
  }
}
